From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: llvm-cygwin <dev@llvm-cygwin.local>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 15:40:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] [lld][COFF] Load automatic imports again after LTO codegen

MinGW automatic imports are prepared by loadMinGWSymbols(), which pulls in
the lazy __imp_<sym> archive member of every undefined <sym>, and that pass
only runs once, before compileBitcodeFiles().

LTO codegen can introduce undefined symbols that did not exist during that
pass, because clang only emits them while compiling the merged bitcode.
For imported data clang does not reference <sym> directly, but emits a
.refptr.<sym> chunk which the linker later rewires to the import address
table.  As the corresponding __imp_<sym> stub is still a lazy archive
symbol at that point, handleMinGWAutomaticImport() finds no Defined symbol
for it and the reference is reported as undefined.

This is the normal case on Cygwin, where the stack protector guard is
imported from cygwin1.dll instead of being defined locally as on MinGW: with
LTO enabled any program instrumented by -fstack-protector fails to link:

  ld.lld: error: undefined symbol: __stack_chk_guard
  >>> referenced by prog.exe.lto.obj:(.refptr.__stack_chk_guard)

Run the automatic import pass once more after the post-LTO run() so that the
stubs introduced by codegen get loaded as well.

Signed-off-by: llvm-cygwin <dev@llvm-cygwin.local>
diff --git a/lld/COFF/Driver.cpp b/lld/COFF/Driver.cpp
index ec1875638..5c088ddb0 100644
--- a/lld/COFF/Driver.cpp
+++ b/lld/COFF/Driver.cpp
@@ -2775,6 +2775,16 @@ void LinkerDriver::linkerMain(ArrayRef<const char *> argsArr) {
   // references to the symbols we use from them.
   run();
 
+  // LTO codegen can introduce undefined symbols that were not present when
+  // the automatic import pass ran above.  Clang emits such a reference for
+  // imported data, e.g. .refptr.__stack_chk_guard for the Cygwin runtime,
+  // and the matching __imp_ stub is still a lazy archive symbol here, so
+  // run the import pass again to pull it in.
+  if (config->autoImport || config->stdcallFixup) {
+    ctx.forEachSymtab([](SymbolTable &symtab) { symtab.loadMinGWSymbols(); });
+    run();
+  }
+
   // Apply symbol renames for -wrap.
   ctx.forEachSymtab([](SymbolTable &symtab) {
     if (!symtab.wrapped.empty())
